WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
The carton says pure milk.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.050
Nothing added, straight from the farm.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.770
But a chemist reads the same
label and shakes their head.

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.930
Milk, they say, isn't pure at all.

5
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.290
And they claim a thermometer
could help prove it.

6
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.270
So who's right, the
label or the chemist?

7
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.570
And how could a temperature
reading settle the argument?

8
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.270
In this mission, you'll find out
what a chemist means by pure.

9
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.890
You'll see how melting and boiling
points can reveal whether a

10
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.470
substance is pure.

11
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.630
And you'll meet formulations,

12
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.630
mixtures designed on
purpose to do a job.

13
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.670
Your mission: decide
what pure really means,

14
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.930
and how to test for it.
